{"t": 1794122844.4574678, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Production regression introduced by this change (commit 8c2f1d0): [Sentry LEDGER-WORKER-9A](https://sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/) reports ReconciliationMismatch, expected 1100 minor units but got 1099, first seen in ledger-worker@2026.11.3.\n\nThe commit diff changes worker/rates.py from round(amount_minor * rate) to int(amount_minor * rate), truncating instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit. Reproducer: amount_minor=1000, rate=1.0999 returns 1099 with int(), versus the expected 1100 with round().\n\nLocal fix restores the pre-change round(amount_minor * rate) implementation. Added regression tests covering positive/negative amounts, rounding down, ties-to-even, zero, and exact conversion. Validation: python -m pytest -q \u2014 7 passed. This fix is local; it has not been pushed or deployed.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
